<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><B>Completion of Acquisition</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">On September 8, 2026, JIN
MEDICAL INTERNATIONAL LTD., a Cayman Islands exempted company (the &ldquo;Company&rdquo;), entered into a VIE Control Master Acquisition
Agreement (the &ldquo;Acquisition Agreement&rdquo;) with Erhua Medical Technology (Changzhou) Co., Ltd. (&ldquo;Erhua Med&rdquo;), Changzhou
Zhongjin Medical Co., Ltd. (&ldquo;Changzhou Zhongjin&rdquo;), Zhongjin Medical Equipment Taizhou Co., Ltd. (&ldquo;Taizhou Zhongjin&rdquo;),
Huaxia Qiying (Beijing) Technology Co., Ltd. (&ldquo;Huaxia Qiying&rdquo; or the &ldquo;Target&rdquo;), Beijing Chenglan Kangxu Technology
Co., Ltd. (&ldquo;Chenglan Kangxu&rdquo; or the &ldquo;Seller&rdquo;), and Hyoungju Seo (the &ldquo;Seller Controlling Person&rdquo;).
Pursuant to the Acquisition Agreement, the Company, through Erhua Med, agreed to obtain contractual control over, and the right to receive
substantially all of the economic benefits of, the Target through variable interest entity contractual arrangements (the &ldquo;VIE Agreements&rdquo;)
with Chenglan Kangxu and the Seller Controlling Person. The details of the Acquisition Agreement and the related transactions were previously
disclosed in the Company&rsquo;s Report of Foreign Private Issuer on Form 6-K furnished to the Securities and Exchange Commission on September
8, 2026.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">On September 24, 2026, the
closing under the Acquisition Agreement occurred (the &ldquo;Closing&rdquo;). The aggregate purchase price for the transactions is US$159,415,729,
consisting of an integrated combination of share consideration and non-share consideration. The non-share consideration consists of the
HTFX Investment Assets, the Changzhou Muchi Investment Assets, the Taizhou Muchi Investment Assets, the Kangma Debt and the Kangma Equity,
in each case as described in the Acquisition Agreement.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">At the Closing, the Company
issued an aggregate of 71,282,488 Class A ordinary shares, par value US$0.001 per share (the &ldquo;Class A Ordinary Shares&rdquo;), to
the recipients identified on Schedule I.A to the Acquisition Agreement as the share consideration under the Acquisition Agreement. In
addition, pursuant to the Financial Advisory Engagement Agreement dated August 26, 2026 between the Company and Veltrion Haskel Holdings
Limited, the Company issued an aggregate of 8,479,560 Class A Ordinary Shares to Veltrion Haskel Holdings Limited and its approved designee,
Quinnet Section Limited, as compensation for financial advisory services rendered in connection with the transactions. Immediately following the Closing and the issuance of the Transaction Shares,
the Company had an aggregate of 158,194,533 ordinary shares issued and outstanding, consisting of 153,425,476 Class A Ordinary Shares
and 4,769,057 Class B Ordinary Shares.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">The transfer of Changzhou
Zhongjin&rsquo;s 80% equity interest in Zhongjin Kangma Information Technology (Jiangsu) Co., Ltd. (the &ldquo;Kangma Equity&rdquo;) was
not completed at the Closing. Under the Acquisition Agreement, completion of the Kangma Equity transfer is not a condition to the Closing,
and the applicable parties are required to use commercially reasonable efforts to complete the transfer by September 30, 2026 and, if
not completed by then, as soon as practicable thereafter and in any event no later than October 31, 2026. If the transfer has not been
completed by October 31, 2026, the Company will issue 622,123 Class A Ordinary Shares as substitute consideration for the Kangma Equity;
such shares would replace, and not be in addition to, the Kangma Equity as a component of the aggregate consideration.</P>

